  "worked_solution": "The square root of a negative number is not a real number, while the square root of a non-negative number is a real number.\n\nLet's look at each square root in turn.\n\n- $\\sqrt{21}$ is the square root of $21,$ which is a non-negative number. So $\\sqrt{21}$ is a real number.\n\n- $\\sqrt{-25}$ is the square root of $-25,$ which is a negative number. So $\\sqrt{-25}$ is not a real number.\n\n- $\\sqrt{10.5}$ is the square root of $10.5,$ which is a non-negative number. So $\\sqrt{10.5}$ is a real number.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
